ce Australia Pacific will receive A$25 million, enabling it to enhance campaigns and engage in lengthy legal battles. This funding represents a transformative approach to how mining revenue supports environmental efforts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/an-australian-mining-heiress-and-her-husband-have-pledged-a120-million-to-10-environmental-groups-including-a25-million-for-greenpeace-following-a-multibillion-dollar-sale-of-family-iron-ore-interests/articleshow/135550665.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/an-australian-mining-heiress-and-her-husband-have-pledged-a120-million-to-10-environmental-groups-including-a25-million-for-greenpeace-following-a-multibillion-dollar-sale-of-family-iron-ore-interests/articleshow/135550665.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-05T01:23:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135550947,imgsize-263893.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NJ homeowner wins $173,000 after court upholds award over a neglected oak tree that crushed her home]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135548627.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable case in New Jersey, a homeowner secured $173,000 in damages after an oak tree, reported multiple times as hazardous, fell and damaged her property. The nearby utility company was found negligent in maintaining the tree. Following a favorable jury ruling, the appeals court affirmed the decision, underscoring the obligation of the utility company to address known risks.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-jersey-woman-warned-authorities-about-an-oak-tree-on-an-adjoining-utility-owned-property-it-later-fell-onto-her-home-and-an-appeals-court-upheld-a-jurys-173000-damages-award/articleshow/135548627.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-jersey-woman-warned-authorities-about-an-oak-tree-on-an-adjoining-utility-owned-property-it-later-fell-onto-her-home-and-an-appeals-court-upheld-a-jurys-173000-damages-award/articleshow/135548627.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-05T00:54:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135550605,imgsize-215197.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida-based cruise ship company promised never-ending voyage, took tens of thousands of dollars from passengers, then abandoned them in Cambodia citing fuel costs]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135550071.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-based-cruise-ship-company-promised-never-ending-voyage-took-tens-of-thousands-of-dollars-from-passengers-then-abandoned-them-in-cambodia-citing-fuel-costs/articleshow/135550071.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-based-cruise-ship-company-promised-never-ending-voyage-took-tens-of-thousands-of-dollars-from-passengers-then-abandoned-them-in-cambodia-citing-fuel-costs/articleshow/135550071.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-05T00:30:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135550806,imgsize-122058.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pennsylvania approves zoning for a $1.4B data center project involving 194 families and 4,466 acres]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135548022.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Salem Township, local officials have greenlighted a significant new zoning plan to establish a technology and energy campus. This ambitious $1.4 billion development will span 4,466 acres, affecting 194 families in the area. Alongside the main project, amenities such as a micro-hospital and recreational spaces are promised to enhance community welfare. However, property transfers will require further environmental assessments and reviews before finalization.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-a-pennsylvania-town-194-families-have-assembled-4466-acres-for-a-potential-1-4-billion-data-centre-deal-officials-approved-new-zoning-but-the-land-sale-and-proposed-12-million-hospital-are-not-final/articleshow/135548022.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-a-pennsylvania-town-194-families-have-assembled-4466-acres-for-a-potential-1-4-billion-data-centre-deal-officials-approved-new-zoning-but-the-land-sale-and-proposed-12-million-hospital-are-not-final/articleshow/135548022.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T23:30:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135548565,imgsize-119722.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Fremont Hindu temple responds to reports of 25 noise complaints, reveals names of Indian couple who apparently filed objection; says 'we attempted to arrange meetings']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135547996.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/fremont-hindu-temple-responds-to-reports-of-25-noise-complaints-reveals-names-of-indian-couple-who-apparently-filed-objection-says-we-attempted-to-arrange-meetings/articleshow/135547996.cms]]></link><guid><![C