DATA[US job openings jump to 7.52 million as layoffs fall, but hiring remains slow]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135544539.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[By September 2026, job vacancies in the United States climbed to an astonishing 7.52 million, demonstrating resilient hiring across various sectors, especially in public services. Interestingly, layoffs dropped while voluntary quits spiked, notably in the accommodation and food services industry. Recent revisions to employment statistics revealed higher job openings and hiring for August 2026. Expect the US Bureau of Labor Statistics to disclose October's numbers on December 1, 2026.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-job-openings-rise-by-333000-to-7-52-million-in-september-while-layoffs-fall-by-127000-fresh-government-data-shows-although-economists-caution-that-the-labor-market-remains-slow-to-hire/articleshow/135544539.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-job-openings-rise-by-333000-to-7-52-million-in-september-while-layoffs-fall-by-127000-fresh-government-data-shows-although-economists-caution-that-the-labor-market-remains-slow-to-hire/articleshow/135544539.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T22:42:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135546956,imgsize-208991.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rare 1867 silver coin made for China trade sells for $4.75 million at Hong Kong auction; collection fetches nearly $32 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135528874.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A rare silver coin, crafted over 150 years ago, fetched an astonishing $4.758 million at a Hong Kong auction. This exceptional piece was part of the proposed Kwan Ping Trade Coinage aimed at solidifying trade currency standards in China. Hidden from public view since the mid-20th century, its mystery adds to its allure.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-rare-silver-coin-pattern-made-in-london-around-1867-for-trade-in-shanghai-spent-decades-in-a-private-collection-it-has-now-sold-for-4-758-million-at-a-hong-kong-auction-leading-a-nearly-32-million-sale/articleshow/135528874.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-rare-silver-coin-pattern-made-in-london-around-1867-for-trade-in-shanghai-spent-decades-in-a-private-collection-it-has-now-sold-for-4-758-million-at-a-hong-kong-auction-leading-a-nearly-32-million-sale/articleshow/135528874.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-05T04:58:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135530155,imgsize-1448816.cms"/></item></channel></rss>